<h1>Euclid's algorithm</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
An algorithm to compute the <a href="greatestCommonDivisor.html"><em>greatest common divisor</em></a> of two positive integers.  It is <tt>Euclid(a,b){if (b=0) then return a; else return Euclid(b, a mod b);}</tt>.  The run time complexity is  <a href="bigOnotation.html"><em>O((log a)(log b))</em></a> bit operations. 
</p>

<p>
<strong>Also known as</strong> Euclidean algorithm.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="binaryGCD.html"><em>binary GCD</em></a>, <a href="extendEuclid.html"><em>extended Euclid's algorithm</em></a>, <a href="fergusonForcade.html"><em>Ferguson-Forcade algorithm</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
After <a href="../terms.html#CLR90">[CLR90, page 810]</a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
Worst-case behavior <a href="https://www.auto.tuwien.ac.at/~blieb/woop/euclid.html" target="_blank">annotated for real time (WOOP/ADA)</a>.

